# BVLL messages that carry an NPDU (Annex J.2.9–J.2.12): what every
# BACnet/IP datagram of application traffic is.

# Who-Is to every network, broadcast on this subnet.
81 0b 00 0c 01 20 ff ff 00 ff 10 08 => original-broadcast npdu 0120ffff00ff1008
# ReadProperty, sent to one device.
81 0a 00 11 01 04 00 05 01 0c 0c 02 00 02 57 19 4d => original-unicast npdu 01040005010c0c02000257194d
# A Who-Is a BBMD relays, from 192.168.1.10:47808 on its subnet.
81 04 00 12 c0 a8 01 0a ba c0 01 20 ff ff 00 ff 10 08 => forwarded from 192.168.1.10:47808 npdu 0120ffff00ff1008
# A foreign device's Who-Is, for its BBMD to distribute.
81 09 00 0c 01 20 ff ff 00 ff 10 08 => distribute-broadcast npdu 0120ffff00ff1008
# An I-Am a BBMD relays from a device on port 47809.
81 04 00 1b 0a 00 00 05 ba c1 01 00 10 00 c4 02 00 02 57 22 05 c4 91 03 22 01 04 => forwarded from 10.0.0.5:47809 npdu 01001000c4020002572205c49103220104
# An empty NPDU is still a message; the NPDU layer refuses it.
81 0a 00 04 => original-unicast npdu (empty)
